{"id":"1c3ecb3059f70f57","group":"72","path":"72/72-df-primitive-recursive-arithmetic.md","title":"df primitive recursive arithmetic","display":"df primitive recursive arithmetic","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Handbook of Proof Theory","book_abbrev":"72","label":"72-df-primitive-recursive-arithmetic","aliases":["72-df-primitive-recursive-arithmetic"],"display":"df primitive recursive arithmetic","depends_on":["[[72-df-peano-arithmetic]]","[[72-df-epsilon-0-notation]]","[[72-df-recursive-order-presentation]]","[[72-df-two-sorted-derivability]]","[[72-df-second-order-arithmetic-syntax]]"],"source_edition":"Buss (ed.), Handbook of Proof Theory, Elsevier, 1998","source_location":"Ch.IV §2.2.2, print264–266/PDF276–278; explicit PRA convention","verification_status":"reviewed-definition","proof_status":"definition-well-defined","eligible_as_verified_dependency":true},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Handbook of Proof Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"72"},{"key":"label","html":"72-df-primitive-recursive-arithmetic"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>72-df-primitive-recursive-arithmetic</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df primitive recursive arithmetic"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"5e5fb64772853785\" href=\"?note=5e5fb64772853785\" title=\"72-df-peano-arithmetic\">72-df-peano-arithmetic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"069c67d72b4fb710\" href=\"?note=069c67d72b4fb710\" title=\"72-df-epsilon-0-notation\">72-df-epsilon-0-notation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9cc4e14a96f221dc\" href=\"?note=9cc4e14a96f221dc\" title=\"72-df-recursive-order-presentation\">72-df-recursive-order-presentation</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"b63a805280ad1d8e\" href=\"?note=b63a805280ad1d8e\" title=\"72-df-two-sorted-derivability\">72-df-two-sorted-derivability</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"5ae195683ce3beb4\" href=\"?note=5ae195683ce3beb4\" title=\"72-df-second-order-arithmetic-syntax\">72-df-second-order-arithmetic-syntax</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Buss (ed.), Handbook of Proof Theory, Elsevier, 1998"},{"key":"source_location","html":"Ch.IV §2.2.2, print264–266/PDF276–278; explicit PRA convention"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"reviewed-definition"},{"key":"proof_status","html":"definition-well-defined"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"true"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>使用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"5e5fb64772853785\" href=\"?note=5e5fb64772853785\" title=\"72-df-peano-arithmetic\">72-df-peano-arithmetic</a> 的 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_{\\rm PR},\\operatorname{Def}_{\\rm PR},B_N,\\operatorname{Ind}_x\">\\(E_{\\rm PR},\\operatorname{Def}_{\\rm PR},B_N,\\operatorname{Ind}_x\\)</span>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\">\\(\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"5ae195683ce3beb4\" href=\"?note=5ae195683ce3beb4\" title=\"72-df-second-order-arithmetic-syntax\">72-df-second-order-arithmetic-syntax</a> 中由 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{QVar}\">\\(\\operatorname{QVar}\\)</span> 定义的无量词一阶片段。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{PRA}\">\\(\\mathsf{PRA}\\)</span> 的演算是 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"b63a805280ad1d8e\" href=\"?note=b63a805280ad1d8e\" title=\"72-df-two-sorted-derivability\">72-df-two-sorted-derivability</a> 的数变量部分。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e\\in\\mathsf{RO}\">\\(e\\in\\mathsf{RO}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e_\\varepsilon\">\\(e_\\varepsilon\\)</span> 为 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"069c67d72b4fb710\" href=\"?note=069c67d72b4fb710\" title=\"72-df-epsilon-0-notation\">72-df-epsilon-0-notation</a> 的固定PR表示，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{TI}_e(A)\">\\(\\operatorname{TI}_e(A)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"9cc4e14a96f221dc\" href=\"?note=9cc4e14a96f221dc\" title=\"72-df-recursive-order-presentation\">72-df-recursive-order-presentation</a>，对数公式该构造也为数公式。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf{PRA}:=B_N\\cup\\operatorname{Def}_{\\rm PR}\\cup\\{\\operatorname{Ind}_x(A):A\\in\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\\land x\\in V_N\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathsf{PRA}:=B_N\\cup\\operatorname{Def}_{\\rm PR}\\cup\\{\\operatorname{Ind}_x(A):A\\in\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\\land x\\in V_N\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{QF\\!TI}(e):=\\{\\operatorname{ucl}(\\operatorname{TI}_{e,x_0}(A)):A\\in\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\\}\\qquad(e\\in\\mathsf{RO}).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{QF\\!TI}(e):=\\{\\operatorname{ucl}(\\operatorname{TI}_{e,x_0}(A)):A\\in\\operatorname{QF}_1(E_{\\rm PR})\\}\\qquad(e\\in\\mathsf{RO}).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>PRA在全部PR函数的定义扩展语言中仅取无量词归纳。它不是字面上PA基本语言内的公理子集；消去PR定义后才得到与PA的有效包含/解释。QFTI(e)是沿给定PR序表示的额外无量词归纳模式；原有QFTI(e_ε)仍是整个ε0次序上的实例，不是PRA已经具有的公理。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"72-df-peano-arithmetic","status":"resolved","id":"5e5fb64772853785","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · de